# Topic 6 · Gender and Governance

::: glance | Topic 6 at a glance
**Head VII** of the syllabus: ==8.5 visits== (eight full questions and one short note, 2016–2025), plus 14 of the 140 MCQs — mostly firsts and numbers. Three families: **quotas** (2016 pros and cons, 2021 results, 2024 impact, 2025 history); **participation** (2017 democracy and development, 2018 "half the sky", 2024 a human right); and **representatives and leaders** (2020 "pull each other up", 2022 issues of women representatives). The suffragist movement was a short note in 2019. Every answer is a **judgement** built on Pitkin, Dahlerup, the quota history and the 2024 election data. Never yet asked in full: defining governance, women as **voters**, and the **South Asian case studies**.
:::

